From 7977c1093a24f0eaa385ce6b0145660982b1dd46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "kevin.krausse" <kkrausse97@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:47:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add first-person Gromen version with bondholder finale
 and one-command build

The narrator now speaks as Gromen, in phrases from his Oct 2 2026 Tree
Rings issue ('mathematical certainty', 'wash, rinse, repeat', 'inflated
away'), with no hedging line. Two requested details are not in that
issue and stay out of the narration: he says 'East Asia', not Japan,
and that the surplus is 'going into gold'. Japan appears as a flag
among the foreign holders instead.

Visuals get their own copy of the choreography: a bondholders row that
bursts and does not reassemble in the finale, China's surplus flowing
into a growing gold orb, flags drawn from primitives (colour emoji only
render in screen-space text), and the caveat beat removed. The header
keeps one label, 'GROMEN'S THESIS / DRAMATIZED'.

build.sh runs voice, plan, stills or full render, package and publish
in one command, and voice.py caches takes so a script edit regenerates
only the lines that changed. The previous round took ~90 minutes for
about ten minutes of real work; this is the fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
